• We introduce a new network architecture named CLFT, employing an innovative progressive-assemble strategy of vision transformers within a double-direction network. • To the best of our knowledge [17] [18], CLFT is the first open-source transformer-based network that directly uses camera and LiDAR sensory input for object semantic segmentation tasks. • We divide datasets based on illumination and weather conditions. This approach allows us to compare and highlight the robustness and efficacy of different models in challenging real-world situations. • We conduct comprehensive benchmark experiments to evaluate the effectiveness of different backbones and input modalities. The results prove that the key-feature of our CLFT models, a combination of transformer and multimodal sensor fusion, has advancements and strengths in all scenarios.
