IV. DATASET CONFIGURATION
The primary purpose of this work is to compare the performance of the vision transformer and CNN backbones for semantic segmentation. Our previous work [16] successfully modeled and evaluated a ResNet50-based FCN to carry out camera-LiDAR fusion. In order to maintain an accordant experiment environment, we construct the input data based on Waymo dataset [53] to evaluate CLFT and other models. Waymo dataset was recorded by multiple high-quality cameras and LiDAR sensors. The scenes of Waymo dataset span various illumination levels, weather conditions, and traffic scenarios. Therefore, we manually partitioned the data sequences into four subsets: light-dry, light-wet, dark-dry, and dark-wet. The light’ and ’dark’ indicate the relative illumination conditions. The ’dry’ and ’wet’ represent the weather difference in precipitation. Table I shows the details of the dataset partition.
